The provided test code has a latent bug due to test case inter-dependency. The global state variables (`first_packet`, `padding`, `header_extension`, `marker`, `zero_payload`, `n_received`) are not reset between test runs. Furthermore, the test suite setup function `rtp_tests_setup` is incorrectly registered as a one-time `setup` function instead of a per-test `before` function. This means the RTP session is not re-initialized for each test case, and state from one test can cause failures in another.

The fix involves two changes:
1.  Modify `rtp_tests_setup` to reset all the global state variables to their default values.
2.  Correct the `ZTEST_SUITE` registration to use `rtp_tests_setup` as the `before` function, ensuring it runs before each test case.

This will ensure each test case runs in a clean, isolated environment.

